module gunbc.namespace_unique_on_chain_policy_scaffold

import std.disposition { Disposition, Scaffold, SingleAuthority }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

data namespace_unique_on_chain_policy_hand_rust_scaffold: Disposition = Scaffold {
  dissolves_to: SingleAuthority,
  bind: DeclarationRef {
    module_path: "test.retirement.namespace_unique_on_chain_policy_retained",
    decl_name: "namespace_unique_on_chain_policy_retention",
    field: WholeDeclaration
  }
}

data namespace_unique_on_chain_policy_hand_rust_dissolve_trigger: String = "DISSOLVE-ON: v1 self-host deletes src/v1 and the host thread-local NameResolutionPolicy gate; dag-native policy witnesses replace src/v1/tests/src/namespace_unique_on_chain_policy_test.rs (hand-Rust LOC after → 0). ROADMAP row: gunbc.roadmap_authority namespace-canonical-binding."

data namespace_unique_on_chain_policy_hand_rust_receipt_plan_anchor: String = "gunbc.roadmap_authority namespace-canonical-binding"

data namespace_unique_on_chain_policy_hand_rust_loc_before: Int = 244

data namespace_unique_on_chain_policy_hand_rust_loc_after: Int = 277

data namespace_unique_on_chain_policy_loc_delta_net: Int = 33

data namespace_unique_on_chain_policy_hand_rust_loc_census_note: String = "Hand-Rust keystone witness LOC census vs origin/main (src/v1/tests/src/namespace_unique_on_chain_policy_test.rs): before=244 after=277 net=+33. Interim growth is counted against ROADMAP row namespace-canonical-binding; dissolve-on deletes the rs (after → 0). A bare plan-filename is not the receipt — the checkable anchor is gunbc.roadmap_authority namespace-canonical-binding."

data namespace_unique_on_chain_policy_cli_run_hand_rust_loc_delta_net: Int = 83

data namespace_unique_on_chain_policy_cli_run_hand_rust_census_note: String = "THE SECOND HAND-RUST FILE THIS WORK GROWS, censused here because the first receipt did not cover it (review 45162). src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run.rs goes 32513 -> 32596 vs origin/main, net +83. It is reported as a delta rather than before/after because whole-file LOC on a 32k-line host module measures the file, not this change — the same shape cli_run_witness_admission_hand_rust_loc_delta_net already uses for the same file.\n\nWHAT GREW AND WHY IT IS HAND-RUST: the bulk is containment_resolve_fn_v1_for_module, which now routes the v1 containment census through the SAME chain+decide authority inference uses (module_path_owner_binding_decide, global_bare_unique_chain_candidate) so zero-on-chain never authorizes a whole-corpus search, including the nearest-ancestor LCP widen. That is the point of the node: one name-decision function rather than two that can disagree. Consolidating onto one authority necessarily grows the caller until the seed itself goes, so this is counted interim growth, not a shrink.\n\nIt cannot be a dag witness today for the reason the retention row already states: the census walks the seed interpreter's own resolution state through a host thread-local policy gate, and a substrate program has no handle to flip that gate. So there is no deleted path to point at and no shrink to claim — the honest receipt is a counted delta with a dissolution trigger, which is what this row is.\n\nDISSOLVE-ON: identical to the sibling census above — v1 self-host deletes src/v1 and with it both this growth and the policy gate it serves (delta -> 0). Checkable anchor: gunbc.roadmap_authority namespace-canonical-binding. See namespace_unique_on_chain_policy_parsed_dag_file_hand_rust_census_note for the third and last hand-Rust file, which carries the PR total."

data namespace_unique_on_chain_policy_parsed_dag_file_hand_rust_loc_delta_net: Int = 14

data namespace_unique_on_chain_policy_parsed_dag_file_hand_rust_census_note: String = "THE THIRD AND LAST HAND-RUST FILE THIS WORK GROWS. Found by enumerating every changed .rs against the generated roster in gunbc.stage0_emit_model rather than by inspecting the files this change was known to touch; the first receipt missed cli_run.rs (review 45162) and the follow-up receipt still missed this one, so the enumeration is the method that closes the class, not a third one-off. src/v1/stage0/src/module_path_index/parsed_dag_file.rs goes 39 -> 53, net +14.\n\nWHAT GREW AND WHY: parse_dag_file collapsed three distinct failure states -- read failed, parse error, parse produced no module -- into a single Option::None, which is the DESIGN section 5 state-space conflation, and it is what made the test-module hygiene bridge report the opaque unlocatable 'parse failed: <rel>' with the real diagnostic discarded. The growth adds parse_dag_file_or_err returning a typed Result that names the cause and the path, and reduces parse_dag_file to a wrapper over it. This is growth that BUYS a located refusal, which is the direction section 5 asks for.\n\nHONEST RESIDUE, NOT CLAIMED FIXED: the Option-returning parse_dag_file wrapper is retained, so callers that have not migrated still discard the cause. This PR converts the caller that needed the located refusal; it does not delete the lossy wrapper. Removing it is a separate migration over the remaining callers.\n\nTOTAL: hand-Rust growth for this PR is +33 (policy witness) +83 (cli_run) +14 (parsed_dag_file) = +130. Two earlier receipts on this PR claimed +33 and then +116; both understated it. src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/test_module_hygiene_bridge.rs also changed but is net 0 lines, so it adds no growth to census. Every other .rs in this diff is generated stage0 output listed in gunbc.stage0_emit_model and is regen product, not hand-maintained -- including std_occurrence_identity.rs, which a review characterized as censused hand-Rust growth and which is in fact generated (stage0_emit_model.dag:65).\n\nDISSOLVE-ON: same trigger as the two censuses above -- v1 self-host deletes src/v1 (delta -> 0). Checkable anchor: gunbc.roadmap_authority namespace-canonical-binding."

